OVERLAP_SEC is the single most consequential value here. Too small and P1s vanish silently. Too large and a few extra rows get re-read each cycle, which costs nothing. When uncertain, go larger. The asymmetry is extreme: the downside of a generous overlap is a rounding error in database load; the downside of a tight one is a missed Sev-1 at a bank.
